    {
      "slug": "the-arrest-of-pangeran-diponegoro",
      "title": "The Arrest of Pangeran Diponegoro",
      "year": 1857,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4f/Raden_Saleh_-_Diponegoro_arrest.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 5255,
      "imageHeight": 3307,
      "story": "The Arrest of Pangeran Diponegoro is the name of an 1857 painting by Raden Saleh, depicting the capture of Prince Diponegoro by Lieutenant General Hendrik Merkus de Kock on 28 March 1830.",
      "facts": [
        "Diponegoro died in 1855, which art historian Werner Krauss suggests inspired the artist to complete The Arrest of Pangeran Diponegoro and \"reformulate\" the arrest in Javanese terms, rather than the colonial terms of Pieneman.",
        "Saleh was also likely inspired by history painters, particularly Louis Gallait; Krauss finds similarities between Gallait's The Abdication of Charles V and Saleh's depiction of Diponegoro's arrest.",
        "Around the early 1970s, The Arrest of Pangeran Diponegoro was given some restoration, including a new coat of varnish.",
        "Owing to the amount of damage the painting had sustained and its historical value, in 2012 the Goethe-Institut and Ansari Djojohadikusumo Foundation arranged for The Arrest of Pangeran Diponegoro to be restored by conservator Susanne Erhards of the Köln Group."
      ],
      "wikipediaUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Arrest_of_Pangeran_Diponegoro",
